# Lake build artifacts
.lake/
/.lake

# Archon state directory
.archon/

# Scratch probe files at the project root.
#
# Throwaway single-file experiments (axiom probes, goal inspection, tactic trials)
# that sessions create beside the library and delete when done. They are NOT part
# of the `AlgebraicJacobian` lib target, so nothing imports or elaborates them and
# a stale one is invisible to every build.
#
# They are ignored because the shared workspace index sweeps whatever sits in the
# tree into whichever commit lands next: a probe created and deleted inside one
# session can be committed by ANOTHER lane's integration commit, and then shows up
# forever afterwards as a phantom staged deletion (inbox `I-0611`). Ignoring the
# pattern is the only fix that does not depend on every session's discipline.
#
# Ported from the sibling project's `.gitignore`, which hardened these patterns on
# 2026-07-28 after a case-sensitive version let `probe_*.lean` through. If a probe
# earns a place in the library, move it under `AlgebraicJacobian/` and import it
# from `AlgebraicJacobian.lean` — do not rename it to dodge this pattern.
#
# SCRATCH DIRECTORIES, added 2026-07-31 (janitor pass, run 0095 r5; inbox `I-1606`).
# The `.lean` patterns above are per-FILE, and every scratch file swept into HEAD so
# far arrived inside a DIRECTORY whose own name carries the marker while the files
# inside it do not: `ScratchPicC/Ax.lean`, `scratch_w7/k1c.lean`,
# `scratch_p4r6_audit/p19_instances2.lean`. Verified in a throwaway repo that the
# sibling's unanchored `*Scratch*.lean` / `*scratch*.lean` pair still does NOT ignore
# those three, and that the two directory patterns below do — including the `.log`
# build dumps that the `.lean` patterns can never reach. Verified also that a normal
# library path such as `AlgebraicJacobian/Curve/P1Curve.lean` stays unignored.
#
# NOTE what ignoring does NOT do: a path already tracked at HEAD stays tracked. The
# 83 scratch paths currently in HEAD must be removed with `git rm --cached` by a lane
# that owns them, and per workspace memory do NOT `add -f` a scratch file to work
# around a refusal — that re-arms it permanently.
*Probe*.lean
*probe*.lean
*Scratch*.lean
*scratch*.lean
*Scratch*/
*scratch*/
/probe_*.lean
/scratch_*.lean
/Scratch_*.lean
